From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: stmmac: dwmac-sun8i: drop received control frames

sun8i_dwmac_set_filter() sets CTL_FRM_FILTER to "receive all control
frames", so every PAUSE frame from the link partner reaches the stack
and is counted in rx_dropped. RX_FLOW_CTL_EN decodes PAUSE frames
either way. Drop control frames, as the vendor driver does.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun8i.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun8i.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun8i.c
index bc668d9..6a438dd 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun8i.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun8i.c
@@ -217,7 +217,6 @@ static const struct emac_variant emac_variant_h6 = {
 
 /* Used in EMAC_RX_FRM_FLT */
 #define EMAC_FRM_FLT_RXALL              BIT(0)
-#define EMAC_FRM_FLT_CTL                BIT(13)
 #define EMAC_FRM_FLT_MULTICAST          BIT(16)
 
 /* Used in RX_CTL1*/
@@ -810,7 +809,8 @@ static void sun8i_dwmac_set_filter(struct mac_device_info *hw,
 	struct netdev_hw_addr *ha;
 	int macaddrs = netdev_uc_count(dev) + netdev_mc_count(dev) + 1;
 
-	v = EMAC_FRM_FLT_CTL;
+	/* drop control frames; RX_FLOW_CTL_EN still acts on PAUSE */
+	v = 0;
 
 	if (dev->flags & IFF_PROMISC) {
 		v = EMAC_FRM_FLT_RXALL;
-- 
Armbian
